redfin 1211: SweetMesa drops sweetfpcd events of an ended op (op-kind rule + generation window, kern.sweet_mesa_stale_ms)

Audit finding 2: sweetfpcd sees a posted Cancel only at its next WAIT + one capture slice, so a cancelled
match could still be translated and unlock the keybag ~250 ms later. Results that do not belong to the kernels running
op kind are dropped; after an op ends, FingerOn/ImageRejected/results carrying the last seen sweetfpcd op_gen are
dropped until a new generation shows up or kern.sweet_mesa_stale_ms (750) passes. fpcd_event.op_gen is S.gen at send
time, so an ended op that sent no event has no known generation (see the comment). kern.sweet_mesa_fix bit 1.
Klog: "dropped stale event: fpcd code N ... gen G (reason; kernel op K, op gen N)".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC4dCbJuYfzxCtCk4D8
---
